## Statuses in use
- `idea` — just thought of it, not committed yet
- `planning` — working out scope & stack
- `building` — under construction
- `testing` — built, being tested
- `live` — actually in use
- `paused` — deliberately on hold
- `archived` — finished / abandoned

## Archived projects
| Project | Ended | Reason | Lesson |
|---|---|---|---|
| claude-terminal | 2026-09-14 | Dropped two days after it started. Built and working — a real terminal on the phone over tmux + Tailscale, 38 server and 12 phone checks — but never once opened on the actual iPhone, and claude-chat already covers the same need well enough. | Three of its four worst bugs were invisible in the code and only appeared when the thing was exercised: a localhost server with no auth could be driven by any website the user visited; a server restart stranded every running session; a launchd job's bare PATH broke the installer. Also: two projects aimed at the same need is one too many — the second was built before the first had been shown to fall short. Code kept private at github.com/juslangit/claude-terminal. |
| kilang | 2026-09-17 | Folded into [gudang](../projects/gudang/00-overview.md) as its generation phase (M7). Opened 2026-09-13, reached planning only — no code was written and its code folder was never created. Gudang covers the same ground from the other end: kilang makes assets, gudang judges and prepares them, and both target Godot and Unreal through the same add-ons. | Two projects aimed at the same need is one too many — the same lesson as claude-terminal, applied this time before either was built rather than after. Notes kept at `projects/kilang/`. |
