# Conventions Across All Projects

> Rules that apply to EVERY project. If one project differs, record the exception
> in that project's `04-methods.md`.

## Language
- Conversation with Claude: English
- Code, variable names, commit messages: English
- Internal documentation (knowledge base): English

## Git
- Branch: `<type>/<short-description>` — e.g. `feat/user-login`, `fix/cart-total`
- Commit: imperative mood, lowercase — e.g. `add user login endpoint`
- Never commit straight to `main`
- Commit identity: `Luqman Hakeem <luqmanh1891@gmail.com>` (set globally on 2026-09-15).
  This is the email linked to the GitHub account `juslangit`, so commits count on the
  contribution graph. Never commit as `academy@todak.com` — it is not linked, and
  commits made with it do not count. Don't set a per-repo email that overrides it.
- On 2026-09-15 every older commit in every repo on GitHub (all branches, plus the local-only
  bluff-show) was re-authored to that identity with `git filter-repo --mailmap` and
  force-pushed, at Luqman's request, so all of his history counts under `juslangit`. The
  old emails were `academy@todak.com`, `luqmanhakeem@todak.com` and
  `juslangit@Luqmans-MacBook-Air.local`. Every commit hash from before that date changed;
  the hashes quoted in the knowledge base were replaced with the new ones. Mirror backups of
  the old history are in `~/Documents/dev/backups/git-rewrite-2026-09-15/`.

## Where things live
- **`~/Desktop/` holds one thing: the `project` folder.** Nothing else goes on the
  Desktop — no scratch files, no downloads, no new folders.
- **`~/Desktop/project/<subject>/<name>/` holds actual projects only,** filed by
  subject: `game/`, `3d/`, `ai/`, `web/` (arranged 2026-09-13). A new subject folder
  is fine when a project fits none of them. Subject folders hold only project
  folders. Tools, dependencies and experiments do not belong there, even when they
  are code and even when they are git repositories.
- **A project may hold other projects** when it is the app they live inside.
  Set 2026-09-22, when `boneka` and `gerak` moved into `3d/bengkel/`, the app
  that holds them both. The nested projects keep their own git repositories,
  their own notes in `~/.claude/knowledge/projects/<name>/`, and their own
  entry in the index; the holder's `.gitignore` excludes them so the two
  histories stay separate. `docs-build` and `docs-site` look two levels deep
  for this reason — before that change both nested records vanished from the
  records site without a word.
- **New projects:** pick the subject from what the project is, tell Luqman which
  folder it's going in, and let him overrule. Pass it as
  `new-project.sh <name> <subject>`.
- claude-chat's phone project list reads the subject folders and shows projects as
  `game/referee-for-fun`. Its LaunchAgent points at `~/Desktop/project/ai/claude-chat`,
  so update the plist if it moves again.
- **Everything else goes in `~/Documents/`.** Development tools live in
  `~/Documents/dev/tools/`, throwaway experiments in `~/Documents/dev/scratch/`.
- Notes for each project stay in `~/.claude/knowledge/projects/<name>/`.
- Before moving a tool, grep `~/.claude.json`, `~/.claude/settings.json` and the
  knowledge base for its absolute path — MCP servers are referenced by full path
  and a move breaks them silently.

