+## Key art
+Use case: illustration-story. Create ONE polished key-art PNG for a funny mobile physics game, exact canvas 1080x1920 pixels, 9:16 portrait, full bleed, no text. Flat 2D storybook cartoon with bold simple shapes, thick warm dark #2a2420 outlines, flat colours plus one soft-edged shadow tone per material, bright warm daylight; clean readable shapes at phone size, no gradients or texture. Scene: grassy tall cliff on RIGHT, a comically wobbly castle of chunky grey-blue stone blocks and warm wooden planks sits at upper RIGHT. Red-and-cream flags. A short round pompous king stands atop highest tower with oversized gold crown, red robe, white fur trim, alarmed eyes looking toward approaching knight. One main floppy ragdoll knight flies diagonally up and RIGHT through open middle-left sky toward the castle: round head in bucket helmet, silver armour, teal tabard, two loose bent arms and two loose bent legs, friendly exuberant expression, harmless slapstick. At bottom LEFT on a green valley floor is the little siege camp with readable wooden catapult that has just launched the knight upward to the right, and a couple tiny red/cream tents. Large airy warm blue sky with soft cream clouds and distant muted rounded green hills. Side-on scene, clear ascending composition from lower-left catapult through flying knight to upper-right king. Grassy plateau around 56% canvas height, cliff drops to valley floor around 88% height. Strong silhouette and negative space between knight and castle. Palette target: sky #87CEE3, grass #8DBF57, cliff #C49468, wood #CD9556, wood shadow #956039, stone #99AFBA, stone shadow #6C8593, armour #DEE4E0, king red #D95543, gold #F4C653, outline #2A2420; cream details. No UI, letters, title, watermark, gore, violence, realistic texture or 3D rendering.
+
+## Sky background
+Use case: illustration-story. Asset: bg-sky.png, a background-only layer for the portrait mobile game Flop Siege. Generate ONE image, 1080x1920 px 9:16 portrait. Input image 1 is STYLE AND PALETTE REFERENCE ONLY. Make a much simpler clean flat 2D storybook background, matching its bright warm daylight, warm blue sky, cream clouds and muted distant green hills. Full frame filled by sky and distant hills. Large calm blue upper sky with just 3 or 4 soft rounded cream cloud groups well spaced; far rounded overlapping hills mostly in lowest third, filled all the way to bottom edge. Flat solid colour fields plus a single gentle shadow colour only, no texture or grain, no painted detailing, no 3D or strong gradients. Background hills low contrast, simple large shapes, dark outlines only where necessary and softer than foreground #2a2420. Preserve ample uncluttered empty sky for airborne knights and towers. STRICT EXCLUSIONS: no castle, no cliff or foreground plateau, no valley floor, no characters, no king or knights, no catapult, no tents, no buildings, no roads, no river, no bridge, no fences, no flags, no UI, no lettering, no watermark. No sun disk. Canvas filled edge to edge. This is only an atmospheric background layer.
+
+## Valley background
+Use case: precise-object-edit. Asset bg-valley.png. Edit input image 1 (the sky background): preserve the SAME sky, exact cloud positions, distant hills, warm daylight and storybook cartoon colours. Output ONE 1080x1920 portrait PNG, 9:16. Add a flat side-on grassy cliff plateau and valley floor as level geometry, with thick warm dark #2a2420 outlines. CRITICAL NORMALIZED GEOMETRY, measured from TOP LEFT: plateau left corner at x=36% (389px), y=56% (1075px). The top silhouette is a PERFECTLY STRAIGHT HORIZONTAL line from (389,1075) to (1080,1075), no perspective slope, no curved crown, no lumps, no grass blades extending above. Plateau mass occupies the RIGHT 64% only. From (389,1075) a near-VERTICAL straight cliff edge descends to (389,1690), so left 36% above floor remains completely OPEN sky and far hills. Warm tan cliff face with just a few broad simple rock shapes in one shadow tone, thin green grass strip at top. Ground floor starts at y=88% (1690px) with a PERFECTLY STRAIGHT HORIZONTAL flat green top, extends all the way from left image edge to right image edge and fills bottom 12% down to bottom edge. Cliff face ends where it joins the valley floor. This is a perpendicular 2D side-on stepped land silhouette, NOT an isometric platform or foreshortened view. Add TWO TINY red-and-cream tents only at extreme lower left x<10% (all tent pixels left of x108), feet on y1690. No other objects. Nothing stands on plateau, no grass tufts above collision edges. All artwork must remain flat clean simple shapes, no fine texture. No castle, buildings besides those two tiny tents, characters, catapult, flags, text, labels, measurement marks, guides, grid, watermark or UI. Preserve background in unoccluded areas. Pixel layout and straight horizontal surfaces take priority over decorative detail.
+
+## Valley placement revision
+Use case: precise-object-edit. Correct ONLY terrain placement and tent size in image 1. Keep its original 941x1672 pixel canvas and identical background clouds and hills. The current plateau is too low: its top is at about row1034. MOVE that perfectly straight horizontal top edge UP to exactly row936 (56% image height). It must start at column339 (36% image width) and end at the right edge. Keep cliff nearly vertical at column339 down to ground. The current floor is too low at row1513: MOVE its perfectly straight horizontal top edge UP to exactly row1472 (88% image height), with green ground filling everything below. Both collision surfaces absolutely level and flat. The tents are too big and spread too far: shrink BOTH so every tent pixel is within the first94 columns (left10%); both feet rest on row1472. Keep bold #2a2420 outlines, green grass and tan cliff, flat cartoon storybook appearance. Keep empty plateau. No new objects, no text, no labels, no guides, no rulers. Do not change sky, clouds or hill composition. Exact placement of the two horizontal ground edges is the sole priority.
+
